<title>POLAND: Most Polish T-bill min prices rise, benchmark flat. [CORRECTED 13:15 GMT]</title>
<headline>Most Polish T-bill min prices rise, benchmark flat. [CORRECTED 13:15 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills rose at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.92 billion zlotys against a 700 million zloty offer, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>The treasury accepted 686 million zlotys (corrects from 243 million zlotys) worth of the bids.  </p>
<p>			 8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    --	95.45    91.11     --	83.53</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.41)  (91.07)    --     (83.53)</p>
<p>   new max price    --	95.70    91.18     --	84.15</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.63)  (91.14)    --     (83.64)</p>
<p>   offer		--	150.0    100.0     --	450.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    --	659.9    418.4     --	839.7</p>
<p>   bids accepted    --	150.0    100.0     --	436.0</p>
<p>   next auction     --	150.0    100.0     --	450.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
